ing NAME = SMITH AND LOCATION = SAN JOSE; LOCATION = SAN JOSE alone matches nothing, because it skips the first key column and the San Jose entries are scattered through the index. A non-matching predicate can still ride along as a search argument; it just does not narrow the scan. \n Source: §3: scans and search arguments; §4: matching index. https://doi.org/10.1145/582095.582099"
